; Pins `:version "9.9.9"` against a manifest declaring
; `:version "1.0.0"`. The filesystem resolver compares the strings
; byte-for-byte and emits plugin_version_mismatch at the (use-plugin
; …) span. Downstream the data form `(circle :r 4)` cannot validate
; because the plugin failed to load — but the diagnostic of interest
; is the resolver-level mismatch; subsequent diagnostics are
; suppressed from the expected output to keep the case focused.
(use-plugin "shapes" :version "9.9.9")
